# Bibliography and local sources (PFE report)

## Download-before-cite

Every reference that appears in the report body or in `biblio.bib` / `\printbibliography` **must** have a corresponding file saved in the workspace **before** you add the `\cite{...}` or the BibTeX entry.

- **Storage:** `reference/sources/`
- **Naming:** `{citekey}.pdf` when the source is a PDF (preferred). Use `{citekey}.html` or `{citekey}.txt` only when no PDF exists but an official full-text page was saved. One primary file per cite key.
- **BibTeX:** Each entry should include a `file = {reference/sources/{citekey}.pdf}` field (or appropriate extension) once the file exists.

## Not usable without a local file

If a paper, report, or page cannot be downloaded and stored under `reference/sources/`, **do not cite it** and **do not add it** to `biblio.bib`. Find an alternative source that can be downloaded, or omit the claim.

Allowed downloads: publisher open access, arXiv, ACL Anthology, institutional repositories, author copies, etc. Do not cite based on metadata alone.

## Workflow

1. Obtain and save the file to `reference/sources/{citekey}.pdf` (or allowed alternative).
2. Add or update the BibTeX entry in `biblio.bib`.
3. Add `\cite{...}` in the LaTeX chapters.

When editing existing cites, verify the matching file still exists under `reference/sources/`.

## Report text (mandatory)

**Never** mention in any report `.tex` content (chapters, introduction, conclusion, annexes, abstracts):

- This download policy or any other Cursor / project workflow rules
- That sources were “stored locally”, “verified offline”, or similar meta-process language

The report must read as normal academic writing only.
